{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And satisfied.</b> With all that he desired to see and to do in his days." "<b>And was gathered to his people.</b> He was gathered to the bond of life, for eternal life, with the righteous of the generations — who are his people and resemble him. The plural 'his people' is used because indeed, though all the righteous merit eternal life, there is great difference in rank among them, as they said, blessed be their memory (Bava Batra 75a): each one is singed by the canopy of his fellow. End of the section חיי שרה."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:37.347960795Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}